# Photos and stored files

The server compresses a photo when it is large. Keep enough quality for the interface, and keep the file small enough that stored files stay lean. Do this on the server. Client files can be altered, so client compression is not the guarantee.

- Limit how many photos each feature may keep. Use a small number that fits the feature.
- Delete objects that are unused, deleted, replaced, uploaded but never attached, or no longer referenced.
- Delete temporary files when the operation finishes, including when it fails.
- Keep objects private. Issue access only to the owner, for a short time.

## Aspect ratio

Each photo slot has a required ratio. If an upload does not match it, fit the whole photo inside that frame. Do not crop it, and do not change its own ratio.

- Compare the photo with the frame. Scale uniformly to the edge that fits, width or height, including scaling up when the photo is smaller.
- Fill the leftover space on the other edge with one shared background color that matches the app surface.
- Split that empty space equally on both sides of the photo.
- Before the upload is sent, the client shows this framed result and states the required ratio. The user can cancel and choose another photo.
- The server stores that same framing. A client preview does not replace the stored file.
